# ResumeX agent rules

- Inspect the existing architecture before modifying code.
- Preserve all existing ResumeX modules and behavior.
- Use TypeScript for all new application code.
- Reuse existing components, schemas, API clients, and visual patterns.
- Never expose API keys in client-side code.
- Keep OpenAI, OpenAlex, Ashby, and database calls server-side.
- Provide a deterministic demo fallback for external API integrations.
- Do not leave placeholder buttons or incomplete flows.
- Before declaring a task complete, run lint, typecheck, tests, and production build.
- Use Playwright to smoke-test important UI flows.
- Check Vercel deployment logs after deployment.
- Do not deploy or push directly to main unless explicitly instructed.
- Never invent candidate qualifications or remove uncertainty labels.
- Prefer official docs (Next.js in `node_modules/next/dist/docs/`, OpenAlex, Ashby) over guesses; use Context7 for library APIs not already in the repo.
